{"term":"spread","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ee422fd160a843f01d","definition":"To stretch out, open out (a material etc.) so that it more fully covers a given area of space.","example":"He spread his newspaper on the table.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["disseminate","circulate","propagate","diffuse","put about"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0f4c2ba69b046588d1","definition":"To extend (individual rays, limbs etc.); to stretch out in varying or opposing directions. simple past and past participle of spread","example":"I spread my arms wide and welcomed him home.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["disseminate","circulate","propagate","diffuse","put about"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b0d3068427da8891b0","definition":"To disperse, to scatter or distribute over a given area.","example":"I spread the rice grains evenly over the floor.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["sow","suffuse","pervade"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:80f35206c09d998a6c","definition":"To proliferate; to become more widely present, to be disseminated.","example":"Whether modern, industrial man is less or more warlike than his hunter-gatherer ancestors is impossible to determine.[…]One thing that is true, though, is that murder rates have fallen over the centuries, as policing has spread and the routine carrying of weapons has diminished. Modern society may not have done anything about war. But peace is a lot more peaceful.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["disseminate","circulate","propagate","diffuse","put about"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:06638d55b76129ef22","definition":"To disseminate; to cause to proliferate, to make (something) widely known or present.","example":"The missionaries quickly spread their new message across the country.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["sweep"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3b5d14623c52a94e21","definition":"To take up a larger area or space; to expand, be extended.","example":"I dropped my glass; the water spread quickly over the tiled floor.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["sweep"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:25bab36bc7467dd163","definition":"To smear, to distribute in a thin layer.","example":"She liked to spread butter on her toast while it was still hot.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["disseminate","circulate","propagate","diffuse","put about"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spread#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"